# Release, handoff, and README SOP (Ledgerly ERP)

**Always ship without asking.** When you finish a connected set of changes that affects **runnable client/server behavior**, **installers**, **packaging**, or **README download docs** — or the user asks for a shipping build / release / hotfix — do the full pipeline below. Do **not** end with “want me to commit/release?”

## Git (required)

1. `git status` — no unintended files (skip secrets, skip `bin/`/`obj/` noise).
2. Commit source + installer script + README + the three `installers\*Setup.exe` when rebuilt.
3. `git push` to the user’s branch (usually `main`). Diagnose push failures; do not end with “you should push.”

## Builds + GitHub Release (required)

1. `dotnet build` Shared → Server → Client **`-c Release`**.
2. Produce **all three** installers via `powershell -File .\build_installers.ps1`:
   - `CoalesceSetup.exe` — combined (Client and/or Server)
   - `CoalesceClientSetup.exe` — client only
   - `CoalesceServerSetup.exe` — server only
3. Bump `MyAppVersion` in `installer/coalesce.iss` when shipping a new tag.
4. Create the next tag (`vX.Y.Z`) and **GitHub Release**, uploading **all three** assets:
   ```powershell
   gh release create vX.Y.Z `
     installers/CoalesceSetup.exe `
     installers/CoalesceClientSetup.exe `
     installers/CoalesceServerSetup.exe `
     --title "vX.Y.Z" `
     --notes "..."
   ```
5. Then update README Downloads (below), commit, push again if needed.
6. If the profile-downloads updater is available, refresh `devildog5x5` README download links (see `profile-downloads-readme-update.mdc`).

## README Downloads (required for a new Release)

1. Update **`README.md` → Downloads** with **verbatim** HTTPS links for **Combined, Client, and Server** on the **same** tag:
   `https://github.com/devildog5x5/ERP/releases/download/{tag}/{asset}`
2. Do not leave Client/Server pointing at a legacy tag when Combined is newer.
3. Refresh latest-release notes (tag links, default login `admin`/`admin`, API `http://127.0.0.1:8000`).
4. **Never invent** working `releases/download/...` URLs. Use `gh release view {tag} --json assets` after upload.
5. Commit and push the README with the release.

## Chat handoff — **### New build links** (every rebuild / release)

Always include **all three** installers (plus release page). Do not omit Client or Server.

| Line | Content |
|------|---------|
| **Combined** | Full URL to `CoalesceSetup.exe` (or Local path if not uploaded) |
| **Client** | Full URL to `CoalesceClientSetup.exe` (or Local path) |
| **Server** | Full URL to `CoalesceServerSetup.exe` (or Local path) |
| **Release page** | `https://github.com/devildog5x5/ERP/releases/tag/{tag}` |
| **Local smoke** | Full paths under `installers\` when built locally |

Do **not** end with “see README” as the only download hint.

## Limits

- Creating tags / uploading release assets needs `gh` auth. If upload fails: still build locally, update README as pending if needed, push commits, and give **exact filenames** + intended URLs for the user to finish upload.
